## Context

Surfaced during ticket 0566/0572 execution (PR #1042): rebuilding the
figures churns 8 committed PDFs byte-wise at identical size — embedded
timestamps (matplotlib `CreationDate` metadata) make the output
non-deterministic. This is reproducibility noise: a clean-room
`make world && git diff --exit-code` oracle would flag spurious diffs,
and every figure-adjacent PR risks committing meaningless churn.

## Actions

1. Set deterministic PDF metadata in the shared plotting helper
   (e.g. `metadata={"CreationDate": None}` on savefig, or
   `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`) — one fix in the shared code path, not per
   script.
2. Rebuild all figures, confirm byte-identical output across two runs.
3. Commit the one-time regeneration if any PDFs change.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Two consecutive figure rebuilds produce byte-identical PDFs
- [ ] `make check` passes
